---
import { CONTRIBUTING, ROADMAP, SPEC } from "../data/links";

const questions = [
    {
        q: "Is it free?",
        a: "Yes. The code is Apache-2.0 or MIT. You pay only for hardware and for any relay you run.",
    },
    {
        q: "Does it work over the internet, or only at home?",
        a: "Both, in 1.0. On one network it connects directly. Across the internet it tries a direct path first. If that fails, it can use a relay you run: a server that forwards the data.",
    },
    {
        q: "Is it safe? Who can see my files?",
        a: "Only the two computers keep the file. The connection is encrypted, and a relay you run passes data without storing it. A ticket is a secret: anyone who has it can fetch the file.",
    },
    {
        q: "What works today?",
        a: "sluice id, sluice doctor and sluice completions. Sending and receiving arrive in 1.0.",
    },
    {
        q: "Do I need a server?",
        a: "Not on one network. Across the internet, a small meeting server called a rendezvous helps the two computers find each other. A relay is needed only when a direct path fails. You run both, and neither keeps the file.",
    },
    {
        q: "What happens if the connection drops?",
        a: "In 1.0, the transfer resumes at the last checked piece. The target is the first new byte within 2 s. Checked data is not sent again.",
    },
    {
        q: "How is it different from the cloud?",
        a: "The file goes straight to the other computer. There is no upload to a company's storage, no account and no plan limit. You keep the only copies.",
    },
    {
        q: "How can I help?",
        a: "Try doctor and say what it prints. Read the spec or the roadmap, or open an issue. Contributions and hard questions are both welcome.",
    },
];
---

<section class="section section-flow faq" id="questions" aria-labelledby="questions-title">
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
            <h2 id="questions-title">Questions</h2>
            <p class="section-lede">
                The short answers. The <a href={SPEC}>specification</a> and the{" "}
                <a href={ROADMAP}>roadmap</a> go further, and{" "}
                <a href={CONTRIBUTING}>contributing</a> says how to help.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-list">
            {questions.map((item) => (
                <details class="faq-item">
                    <summary>{item.q}</summary>
                    <p>{item.a}</p>
                </details>
            ))}
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
